sentences.text:
As far as the offence punishable under Section 420 of IPC is concerned, to constitute the said offence there must be deception i.e., the accused must have deceived someone; that by such deception the accused must induce a person:
(i) to deliver any property; or (ii) to make, alter, destroy a whole or part of the valuable security or anything which is signed or sealed and which is capable of being converted into a valuable property;
or (iii) that the accused must have done so dishonestly.
